e values that can be represented by `Fin n` with an initial value, starting at `0` and\nnesting to the left.\n\nExample:\n * `Fin.foldl 3 (· + ·.val) (0 : Nat) = ((0 + (0 : Fin 3).val) + (1 : Fin 3).val) + (2 : Fin 3).val`\n","docLink":"./Init/Data/Fin/Fold.html#Fin.foldl","kind":"def","line":20,"name":"Fin.foldl","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/470d5ce1400764999581fd26d5d72b00d990b0f4/src/Init/Data/Fin/Fold.lean#L20-L29"}}],"imports":["Init.Control.Lawful.Basic","Init.Data.Fin.Lemmas","Init.Data.Nat.Lemmas","Init.Ext","Init.Hints","Init.Omega","Init.TacticsExtra","Init.WFTactics"],"instances":[],"name":"Init.Data.Fin.Fold"}